RE-EVALUATE AND ADAPT THE DESIGN:

Farmers supplying more than 500 litres in ten days receive an additional ₹0.50 per litre.
The original SNF adjustment remains ₹0.30 per 0.1% unless the co-operative announces a revision.

IMPACT ANALYSIS:

Rate constants must support multiple seasons.
Fat and SNF step calculations must account for two-decimal readings.
The payment function must apply the appropriate season.
A ten-day aggregation function must calculate each farmer's total litres.
A bonus function must add ₹0.50 per litre if the farmer's ten-day quantity is greater than 500 litres.
